ot is now over 3x faster, 22% cheaper, and finds 10% more bugs. The average review time dropped from ~5 minutes to ~90 seconds. Performance gains are powered by Composer 2.5 training progress.\",\n    35→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    36→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    37→    \"date\": \"2026-06-10\",\n    38→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    39→  },\n    40→  {\n    41→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    42→    \"title\": \"Cursor SDK Enhancements - Custom Tools and Auto-Review\",\n    43→    \"description\": \"Released new functionality across TypeScript and Python SDKs including custom stores (SQLite and JSONL), custom tools via function definitions, auto-review for local agents, and nested subagents support. Includes reliability and performance fixes for production use.\",\n    44→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    45→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    46→    \"date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    47→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    48→      {\n    49→        \"quote\": \"Independent PSF assessment of Cursor SDK 3.7 covers custom tools implementation, auto-review functionality for headless runs, nested subagents, and JSONL stores\",\n    50→        \"source\": \"Production AI Institute\",\n    51→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n    52→      }\n    53→    ]\n    54→  },\n    55→  {\n    56→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n    57→    \"title\": \"Codex App 26.608 - Migration Flows and Plugin Revamp\",\n    58→    \"description\": \"Added 'Migrate to Codex' flows for importing setups from Claude Code and Claude Cowork during onboarding. Revamped plugins screen with separate tabs, marketplace filters, keyboard navigation, and clearer install actions. Expanded Settings search across more panels.\",\n    59→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    60→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog?type=codex-cli\",\n    61→    \"date\": \"2026-06-09\",\n    62→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    63→  },\n    64→  {\n    65→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n    66→    \"title\": \"Sites Feature Preview - Build and Deploy Websites\",\n    67→    \"description\": \"Sites is now available in preview in the Codex app, allowing users to create, save, deploy, and inspect websites, dashboards, internal tools, web apps, and games hosted by OpenAI. ChatGPT Business workspaces include Sites by default.\",\n    68→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    69→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog?type=codex-cli\",\n    70→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n    71→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    72→  },\n    73→  {\n    74→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n    75→    \"title\": \"Amazon Bedrock Support\",\n    76→    \"description\": \"Codex can now use supported OpenAI models available through Amazon Bedrock. Users can configure Amazon Bedrock as their model provider to run Codex locally with AWS-managed authentication, account controls, and billing.\",\n    77→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    78→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog?type=codex-cli\",\n    79→    \"date\": \"2026-06-01\",\n    80→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n    84→    \"title\": \"Terminal Placement Controls\",\n    85→    \"description\": \"Added 'Default terminal location' in General settings. When the bottom panel is enabled, users can choose whether terminal shortcuts and environment actions open in the bottom panel or right panel.\",\n    86→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog?type=codex-cli\",\n    88→    \"date\": \"2026-06-01\",\n    89→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    90→  },\n    91→  {\n    92→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n    93→    \"title\": \"Gemini CLI Discontinuation Announcement\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Google announced that Gemini CLI will be discontinued on June 18, 2026 for all user t