"author\": \"AI Con USA\",\n    \"source\": \"Industry Conference\",\n    \"url\": \"https://aiconusa.com/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-development\", \"industry-standards\", \"education\", \"prompt-engineering\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode to Prevent Data Exfiltration\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenAI rolled out Lockdown Mode for eligible accounts to help prevent the final stage of data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. The feature directly attacks the 'exfiltration vectors' leg of the Lethal Trifecta (private data access + untrusted content exposure + data theft transmission). Simon Willison notes this implies ChatGPT's default settings don't provide robust protection against determined data exfiltration attacks.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-05\",\n    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"prompt-injection\", \"llms\", \"openai\", \"lethal-trifecta\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  }\n]",
