      <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-01</span>\n   367→                        </div>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→\n   370→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   371→                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n   372→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   373→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/1-0\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor 1.0 - BugBot, Background Agent & One-Click MCP</a>\n   374→                        </div>\n   375→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   376→                            Cursor's first stable major release. Features include BugBot for automatic code review and bug fixing, Background Agent, Memories feature, One-Click MCP setup with OAuth support, and deep Jupyter Notebook integration.\n   377→                        </div>\n   378→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   379→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-04</span>\n   380→                        </div>\n   381→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   382→                            \"Cursor reached $100 million ARR in June 2025, making it one of the fastest software products to achieve this milestone\"\n   383→                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Industry news - Positive</span>\n   384→                        </div>\n   385→                    </div>\n   386→\n   387→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   388→                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-feature\">Feature</div>\n   389→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   390→                            <a href=\"https://changelog.continue.dev/\" target=\"_blank\">Continue - Enhanced MCP Support</a>\n   391→                        </div>\n   392→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   393→                            v1.0.12 for VS Code and v1.0.21 for JetBrains with enhanced Model Context Protocol (MCP) support including SSE and Streamable HTTP transports for remote hosting.\n   394→                        </div>\n   395→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   396→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-13</span>\n   397→                        </div>\n   398→                    </div>\n   399→\n   400→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   401→                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n   402→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   403→                            <a href=\"https://medium.com/data-and-beyond/rewriting-the-command-line-how-google-gemini-cli-is-turning-terminals-into-ai-powered-super-tools-01d95161bc59\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI - Open-Source AI for Terminals</a>\n   404→                        </div>\n   405→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   406→                            Google launched Gemini CLI as an open-source command-line interface that brings Gemini AI capabilities directly into terminal environments.\n   407→                        </div>\n   408→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   409→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-25</span>\n   410→                        </div>\n   411→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   412→                            \"Gemini CLI 'changes everything for developers' - turning terminals into 'AI-powered super tools'\"\n   413→                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Medium - Positive</span>\n   414→                        </div>\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→\n   417→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   418→                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n   419→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   420→                           