ing against big AI lock-in.\n   446→                        </div>\n   447→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   448→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">TechCrunch</span>\n   449→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-10</span>\n   450→                        </div>\n   451→                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   452→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai-coding</span>\n   453→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">startups</span>\n   454→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">developer-tools</span>\n   455→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">venture-capital</span>\n   456→                        </div>\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→\n   459→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   460→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   461→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode</a>\n   462→                        </div>\n   463→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   464→                            OpenAI rolled out Lockdown Mode to help prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. Directly attacks the 'exfiltration vectors' leg of the Lethal Trifecta.\n   465→                        </div>\n   466→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   467→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   468→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-05</span>\n   469→                        </div>\n   470→                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   471→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">security</span>\n   472→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">prompt-injection</span>\n   473→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llms</span>\n   474→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">openai</span>\n   475→                        </div>\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→\n   478→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   479→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   480→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Enthusiasts vs Skeptics</a>\n   481→                        </div>\n   482→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   483→                            Charity Majors captures the dynamic: enthusiasts race against discontinuous capability leaps creating existential threats, while skeptics race against entropy as faster code shipping degrades reliability.\n   484→                        </div>\n   485→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   486→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison (quoting Charity Majors)</span>\n   487→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-04</span>\n   488→                        </div>\n   489→                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   490→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai</span>\n   491→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">engineering</span>\n   492→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">organizational-design</span>\n   493→                        </div>\n   494→                    </div>\n   495→\n   496→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   497→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   498→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Uber Caps AI Tool Usage at $1,500 Monthly</a>\n   499→                        </div>\n   500→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   501→                            After blowing through its 2026 AI budget in four months, Uber limits employees to $1,500 monthly per AI coding tool. Values AI tools at ~11% of median engineer compensation.\n   502→                        </div>\n   503→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   504→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   505→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-03</span>\n   506→                        </div>\n   507→                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   508→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai</span>\n   509→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llms</span>\n   510→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llm-pricing</span>\n   511→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">coding-agents</span>\n   512→                        </div>\n   513→                    </div>\n   514→\n   515→                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n   516→                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n   517→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Announces MAI-Thinking-1 and MAI-Code-1-Flash</a>\n   518→                        </div>\n   519→                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n   520→                            Microsoft released MAI-Thinking-1 (1T params, 35B active) claimed preferred to Sonnet 4.6, and MAI-Code-1-Flash (137B params, 5B active) for GitHub Copilot. Both trained on 'clean and appropriately licensed' data.\n   521→                        </div>\n   522→                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n   523→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   524→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-02</span>\n   525→                        </div>\n   526→                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   527→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llm-release</span>\n   528→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">generative-ai</span>\n   529→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">microsoft</span>\n   530→                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">training-data</span>\n   531→                        </div>\n   532→                    </div>\n   533→\n   534→                </section>\n   535→            </div>\n   536→        </div>\n   537→    </main>\n   538→\n   539→    <footer>\n   540→        <div class=\"container\">\n   541→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated: 2026-06-12</p>\n   542→            <p>\n   543→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n   544→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Product Updates</a> |\n   545→                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a>\n   546→            </p>\n   547→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 11px;\">\n   548→                Daily research compilation of agentic coding tools, product updates, and technical insights\n   549→            </p>\n   550→        </div>\n   551→    </footer>\n   552→</body>\n   553→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
