ta exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. Directly attacks the 'exfiltration vectors' leg of the Lethal Trifecta.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-05</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">prompt-injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llms</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">openai</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Enthusiasts vs Skeptics</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Charity Majors captures the dynamic: enthusiasts race against discontinuous capability leaps creating existential threats, while skeptics race against entropy as faster code shipping degrades reliability.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison (quoting Charity Majors)</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">organizational-design</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Uber Caps AI Tool Usage at $1,500 Monthly</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            After blowing through its 2026 AI budget in four months, Uber limits employees to $1,500 monthly per AI coding tool. Values AI tools at ~11% of median engineer compensation.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-03</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llms</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llm-pricing</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">coding-agents</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Announces MAI-Thinking-1 and MAI-Code-1-Flash</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Microsoft released MAI-Thinking-1 (1T params, 35B active) claimed preferred to Sonnet 4.6, and MAI-Code-1-Flash (137B params, 5B active) for GitHub Copilot. Both trained on 'clean and appropriately licensed' data.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n        