">enterprise</span>\n   800→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">governance</span>\n   801→                        </div>\n   802→                    </div>\n   803→\n   804→                    <!-- Insight 4 -->\n   805→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   806→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   807→                            <a href=\"https://lalatenduswain.medium.com/top-10-ai-coding-cli-tools-in-2026-a-complete-developers-guide-3c63221bc83e\" target=\"_blank\">Top 10 AI Coding CLI Tools</a>\n   808→                        </div>\n   809→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   810→                            Comprehensive guide covering the AI coding CLI landscape with decision framework for developers, feature comparison, and tool selection guidance.\n   811→                        </div>\n   812→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   813→                            <span class=\"tag\">Medium</span>\n   814→                            <span class=\"date\">2026-06-08</span>\n   815→                        </div>\n   816→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   817→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   818→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">cli-tools</span>\n   819→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">developer-tools</span>\n   820→                        </div>\n   821→                    </div>\n   822→\n   823→                    <!-- Insight 5 -->\n   824→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   825→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   826→                            <a href=\"https://hackaday.com/2026/06/08/revisiting-using-ai-coding-assistants-youre-holding-it-wrong-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Coding Best Practices</a>\n   827→                        </div>\n   828→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   829→                            Developer discussion on proper usage patterns for AI coding assistants and common mistakes developers make when integrating AI tools into workflows.\n   830→                        </div>\n   831→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   832→                            <span class=\"tag\">Hackaday</span>\n   833→                            <span class=\"date\">2026-06-08</span>\n   834→                        </div>\n   835→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   836→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   837→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">best-practices</span>\n   838→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">workflow</span>\n   839→                        </div>\n   840→                    </div>\n   841→\n   842→                    <!-- Insight 6 -->\n   843→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   844→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   845→                            <a href=\"https://aiconusa.com/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Con USA 2026</a>\n   846→                        </div>\n   847→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   848→                            Coverage from AI Con USA featuring workshops on Model Context Protocol Fundamentals and Prompt Engineering for Software Practitioners.\n   849→                        </div>\n   850→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   851→                            <span class=\"tag\">Conference</span>\n   852→                            <span class=\"date\">2026-06-08</span>\n   853→                        </div>\n   854→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   855→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-development</span>\n   856→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">industry-standards</span>\n   857→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">education</span>\n   858→                        </div>\n   859→                    </div>\n   860→\n   861→                    <!-- Insight 7 -->\n   862→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   863→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   864→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Lockdown Mode</a>\n   865→                        </div>\n   866→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   867→                            OpenAI rolled out Lockdown Mode to prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests.\n   868→                        </div>\n   869→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   870→                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   871→                            <span class=\"date\">2026-06-05</span>\n   872→                        </div>\n   873→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   874→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   875→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   876→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   877→                        </div>\n   878→                    </div>\n   879→                </div>\n   880→            </section>\n   881→        </div>\n   882→    </main>\n   883→\n   884→    <footer id=\"about\">\n   885→        <div class=\"container\">\n   886→            <div class=\"footer-info\">\n   887→                <p>Generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK</p>\n   888→                <p class=\"text-small mt-1\">Report Date: 2026-06-12 | Research Cycle: Daily Update</p>\n   889→            </div>\n   890→            <div class=\"footer-links\">\n   891→                <a href=\"#new\">New Products</a>\n   892→                <a href=\"#updates\">Product Updates</a>\n   893→                <a href=\"#insights\">Technical Insights</a>\n   894→            </div>\n   895→        </div>\n   896→    </footer>\n   897→\n   898→    <script>\n   899→        // Smooth scrolling for navigation links\n   900→        document.querySelectorAll('a[href^=\"#\"]').forEach(anchor => {\n   901→            anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {\n   902→                const href = this.getAttribute('href');\n   903→                if (href !== '#') {\n   904→                    e.preventDefault();\n   905→                    const target = document.querySelector(href);\n   906→                    if (target) {\n   907→                        target.scrollIntoView({\n   908→                            behavior: 'smooth',\n   909→                            block: 'start'\n   910→                        });\n   911→                    }\n   912→                }\n   913→            });\n   914→        });\n   915→\n   916→        // Add visited state styling for links\n   917→        document.querySelectorAll('.item-title a').forEach(link => {\n   918→            // Check if link has been visited before (local storage)\n   919→            const url = link.href;\n   920→            if (localStorage.getItem(`visited-${url}`)) {\n   921→                link.style.color = '#828282';\n   922→            }\n   923→\n   924→            link.addEventListener('click', function() {\n   925→                localStorage.setItem(`visited-${url}`, 'true');\n   926→            });\n   927→        });\n   928→\n   929→        // Dynamic date update\n   930→        const today = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];\n   931→        console.log('Report Date:', today);\n   932→    </script>\n   933→</body>\n   934→</html>"
